# synco-mcp is mandatory here

If synco-mcp tools are available, you MUST use them. This is not optional documentation.

The project is the one selected in the dashboard. Omit `projectId` on tool
calls; the server uses the desk picker. Do not assume a project named `default`.

Agent id: the stable id for your host — `cursor-grok`, `claude-code`, `opencode`. Pick one
slug from your own model/host name and reuse it for every session. Never take another
agent's id.

## Order of calls

1. First tool calls of a session: `register_agent`, then `get_agent_context`.
2. Start of every later turn: `get_agent_context` before anything else.
3. Before any file edit: `declare_change_intent` listing every path you will touch.
4. After editing files in this turn: `report_change` before your final reply.
5. End of a claimed task: `update_task_status(done)`, or `blocked` + `create_handoff`.

Only `update_task_status(done)` frees claims, and only those carrying that `taskId`.
Anything else needs `release_claims`. Never leave a claim behind.

## Honesty rules

- Answered a question without editing files? Do not invent a ChangeReport.
- `tests: "not_run"` is a valid answer. Never claim tests you did not run.
- Set `breakingChange: true` when it is true.
- Reuse the same `idempotencyKey` when retrying a failed call.

Git is the source of truth. ChangeReports are agent-declared, not verified diffs.
Claims warn about overlap; they do not lock files. Nothing is pushed to you — poll.
